sam.rivera: decision: snapshot access reviews, change approvals, and backup tests
weekly, timestamp them, and drop them straight into the auditor portal.
sam.rivera: every SOC 2 trust-services criterion gets a named owner before
fieldwork so nothing is orphaned when the auditor asks who owns it.
sam.rivera: next check-in in two weeks to review the shrinking evidence backlog.
NOTE

seed gmail ask-gmail-0004 "Board update — audit status" email 2026-06-05 <<'NOTE'
A short update on our audit posture. We are on track for the SOC 2 Type II
observation window to close on schedule. The evidence backlog that worried me
last quarter is now largely automated — access reviews, change approvals, and
logging retention all generate their own trail without a human chasing
screenshots. The automation investment is already paying for itself in reduced
