NOTE

seed manual ask-note-0006 "Larkspur security controls cheatsheet" note 2026-03-30 <<'NOTE'
A one-page reference for the controls we care about most. Access management: SSO
everywhere, quarterly access reviews, no shared accounts. Change management: every
production change rides a pull request with a second reviewer and an automated
deploy record. Logging: ninety-day retention minimum, centralized and
tamper-evident. Vendor management: a signed security addendum and a current
attestation before any vendor touches customer data. The value is in doing this
consistently and being able to show the evidence on demand.
NOTE

